   "f0": 143.859,
   "st": 2.022,
   "range_st": 8.624,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "s": 9.656,
   "e": 13.469,
   "text": "Go back to the Hebbian memory from chapter four:",
   "dur": 3.814,
   "voiced": 219,
   "sim": 0.776,
   "f0": 113.521,
   "st": -2.078,
   "range_st": 7.442,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "s": 13.614,
   "e": 21.992,
   "text": "the matrix that stores associations by adding up outer products, value times key-transpose.",
   "dur": 8.378,
   "voiced": 385,
   "sim": 0.854,
   "f0": 123.626,
   "st": -0.602,
   "range_st": 7.707,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "s": 22.617,
   "e": 25.149,
   "text": "We watched it drown in crosstalk.",
   "dur": 2.533,
   "voiced": 140,
   "sim": 0.787,
   "f0": 113.138,
   "st": -2.137,
   "range_st": 5.054,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "s": 25.849,
   "e": 28.654,
   "text": "Now look closely at a Transformer.",
   "dur": 2.804,
   "voiced": 159,
   "sim": 0.776,
   "f0": 122.89,
   "st": -0.705,
   "range_st": 8.589,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "s": 29.231,
   "e": 31.955,
   "text": "Strip the softmax out of attention,",
   "dur": 2.724,
   "voiced": 126,
   "sim": 0.785,
   "f0": 125.943,
   "st": -0.28,
   "range_st": 7.958,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "s": 32.489,
   "e": 35.578,
   "text": "and something extraordinary is left behind.",
   "dur": 3.089,
   "voiced": 187,
   "sim": 0.87,
   "f0": 115.822,
   "st": -1.731,
   "range_st": 6.835,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "s": 35.798,
   "e": 42.853,
   "text": "Every new token writes its value, times its key-transpose, into a running matrix.",
   "dur": 7.055,
   "voiced": 415,
   "sim": 0.845,
   "f0": 125.15,
   "st": -0.39,
   "range_st": 8.628,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "s": 43.342,
   "e": 48.289,
   "text": "Every query reads from that matrix, by multiplication.",
   "dur": 4.947,
   "voiced": 260,
   "sim": 0.851,
   "f0": 119.312,
   "st": -1.217,
   "range_st": 9.593,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "s": 49.228,
   "e": 51.311,
   "text": "That is Hebb's rule.",
   "dur": 2.084,
   "voiced": 102,
   "sim": 0.74,
   "f0": 120.997,
   "st": -0.974,
   "range_st": 9.202,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "s": 51.531,
   "e": 52.585,
   "text": "Exactly.",
   "dur": 1.054,
   "voiced": 50,
   "sim": 0.552,
   "f0": 103.804,
   "st": -3.627,
   "range_st": 2.858,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "s": 53.633,
   "e": 61.56,
   "text": "In 2021, Imanol Schlag, Kazuki Irie and J\u00fcrgen Schmidhuber proved it formally.",
   "dur": 7.927,
   "voiced": 438,
   "sim": 0.877,
   "f0": 123.318,
   "st": -0.645,
   "range_st": 6.64,
   "asr": 0.8,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "s": 61.78,
   "e": 65.678,
   "text": "Linear attention is a fast weight programmer:",
   "dur": 3.898,
   "voiced": 214,
   "sim": 0.862,
   "f0": 123.429,
   "st": -0.63,
   "range_st": 9.079,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "s": 65.968,
   "e": 73.817,
   "text": "a slow network that learns, by gradient descent, to write fast synaptic weights while it is thinking.",
   "dur": 7.849,
   "voiced": 396,
   "sim": 0.865,
   "f0": 131.294,
   "st": 0.44,
   "range_st": 8.412,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "s": 75.335,
   "e": 79.318,
   "text": "The idea is older than the Transformer itself.",
   "dur": 3.983,
   "voiced": 231,
   "sim": 0.841,
   "f0": 122.505,
   "st": -0.76,
   "range_st": 5.28,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "s": 80.046,
   "e": 88.951,
   "text": "In 2016, Jimmy Ba and Geoffrey Hinton argued that brains have synapses that change faster than learning,",
   "dur": 8.905,
   "voiced": 482,
   "sim": 0.888,
   "f0": 129.326,
   "st": 0.178,
   "range_st": 8.905,
   "asr": 0.895,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "s": 89.375,
   "e": 91.523,
   "text": "but slower than thought,",
   "dur": 2.149,
   "voiced": 86,
   "sim": 0.762,
   "f0": 115.235,
   "st": -1.819,
   "range_st": 5.856,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "s": 92.143,
   "e": 98.913,
   "text": "and that these fast weights are a neurally plausible way to attend to the recent past.",
   "dur": 6.769,
